;; OCaml's subsets for GT8.4's rotation (O8, doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, "As built: O8 (write-ahead)"; doc/GATE-SURVEY.md, GTS202 (a),
;; GTS205 (a)): the programs bin/gate --nightly runs every night of the AOT levels' parts (oi-aot.run, oi-suite-aot.suite), the rest a
;; seventh a night. Each subset: the negative control's two programs (test/ocaml/controls.txt), one program of each class the level's
;; record holds but the speed classes (a timeout costs the night two minutes; the rotation runs them), and a spread of passing ones
;; (the run corpus: the effects directory, OC67's; the suite: one load program per opam package, and the first of a few directories).
;; Ids as the records write them (test/ocaml/check-aot.edn, check-suite-aot.edn): no part prefix (OC161). Not a coverage subset yet
;; (GTS205's block rule needs oi's and the light level's coverage, OC162). Read with the Clojure reader.
